1
00:00:00,170 --> 00:00:03,390
So there are other duties of directors under

2
00:00:03,390 --> 00:00:04,190
CAMA 2020.

3
00:00:04,690 --> 00:00:07,109
CAMA 2020 is the Communist and Allied Matters

4
00:00:07,109 --> 00:00:07,390
Act.

5
00:00:07,930 --> 00:00:11,510
These duties include that directors are reminded that

6
00:00:11,510 --> 00:00:13,790
they are trustees of the company and as

7
00:00:13,790 --> 00:00:16,070
such they should manage the property of the

8
00:00:16,070 --> 00:00:18,290
company in its best interest.

9
00:00:18,970 --> 00:00:20,970
They have the responsibility of ensuring the accuracy

10
00:00:20,970 --> 00:00:25,230
of the financial statements and this duty cannot

11
00:00:25,230 --> 00:00:26,350
be delegated.

12
00:00:26,770 --> 00:00:29,370
So whilst the CFO has been appointed by

13
00:00:29,370 --> 00:00:31,770
the board to oversee the integrity of the

14
00:00:31,770 --> 00:00:35,310
financial statements, that responsibility remains with the board.

15
00:00:35,750 --> 00:00:38,570
It cannot abdicate that responsibility.

16
00:00:39,570 --> 00:00:42,230
Directors also have a responsibility to the environment

17
00:00:42,230 --> 00:00:44,070
and I think this is more so now

18
00:00:44,070 --> 00:00:47,390
that there's a lot of conversation around ESG

19
00:00:47,390 --> 00:00:50,470
and matters relating to taking care of the

20
00:00:50,470 --> 00:00:50,990
environment.

21
00:00:52,070 --> 00:00:55,110
The board has a responsibility to measure and

22
00:00:55,110 --> 00:00:56,170
monitor performance.

23
00:00:56,890 --> 00:00:59,150
It has to measure its own performance.

24
00:00:59,750 --> 00:01:02,570
Typically the board will set key performance indicators

25
00:01:02,570 --> 00:01:05,970
against which its performance will be measured per

26
00:01:05,970 --> 00:01:06,410
period.

27
00:01:07,330 --> 00:01:10,550
It can set such performance indicators as oversights

28
00:01:10,550 --> 00:01:14,550
of succession planning, oversights of KPIs for management,

29
00:01:15,270 --> 00:01:17,610
oversights of so many things and then at

30
00:01:17,610 --> 00:01:19,310
the end of the year it can measure

31
00:01:19,310 --> 00:01:20,590
how well it has done.

32
00:01:21,130 --> 00:01:23,410
But under this head the most critical responsibility

33
00:01:23,410 --> 00:01:25,750
of the board is to measure the performance

34
00:01:25,750 --> 00:01:28,590
of management and typically what the board does

35
00:01:28,590 --> 00:01:31,010
or should do is to set key performance

36
00:01:31,010 --> 00:01:33,950
indicators not just financial because a lot of

37
00:01:33,950 --> 00:01:38,530
boards unfortunately end up setting only financial indicators.

38
00:01:39,410 --> 00:01:42,830
Typically they set a budget and if the

39
00:01:42,830 --> 00:01:45,890
budget is achieved it's heuristic to management.

40
00:01:46,150 --> 00:01:49,350
However, an effective board should go beyond setting

41
00:01:49,350 --> 00:01:52,030
financial indicators for management.

42
00:01:52,350 --> 00:01:56,870
So things like staff attrition, stakeholder engagements, even

43
00:01:56,870 --> 00:02:01,230
engagement with the board itself, leadership alignments, oversight

44
00:02:01,230 --> 00:02:04,270
of strategy would go into the CEO's appraisal

45
00:02:04,270 --> 00:02:07,389
and the CEO would also cascade this to

46
00:02:07,389 --> 00:02:09,410
his own reports including the EEDs.

47
00:02:10,230 --> 00:02:12,570
And beyond setting the KPIs the board also

48
00:02:12,570 --> 00:02:14,610
has to put in place a process for

49
00:02:14,610 --> 00:02:19,530
measuring, for appraising performance against the KPIs that

50
00:02:19,530 --> 00:02:20,250
has been set.

51
00:02:20,850 --> 00:02:23,430
The board also has a responsibility to define

52
00:02:23,430 --> 00:02:26,870
a remuneration policy for itself, that is for

53
00:02:26,870 --> 00:02:30,490
directors as well as for executive management.

54
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:33,910
And most of the time there's a portion

55
00:02:33,910 --> 00:02:36,910
of executive management remuneration that is linked to

56
00:02:36,910 --> 00:02:39,890
performance which is why setting KPIs and measuring

57
00:02:39,890 --> 00:02:41,390
the KPIs is critical.

58
00:02:44,300 --> 00:02:47,100
Further going into the duties and responsibilities is

59
00:02:47,100 --> 00:02:49,140
one for ensuring that there's a risk management

60
00:02:49,140 --> 00:02:50,240
framework in place.

61
00:02:51,000 --> 00:02:53,240
The board has to define the risk appetite

62
00:02:53,240 --> 00:02:55,920
and the risk capacity as well as the

63
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:57,520
risk limits of the organisation.

64
00:02:58,140 --> 00:03:00,520
In this regard an enterprise risk management framework

65
00:03:00,520 --> 00:03:04,700
is in place and that is monitored per

66
00:03:04,700 --> 00:03:05,160
period.

67
00:03:05,660 --> 00:03:07,620
Reports in this regard are expected to be

68
00:03:07,620 --> 00:03:10,820
presented to the board at its quarterly meetings.

69
00:03:11,700 --> 00:03:13,860
The board also has oversight of risk governance

70
00:03:13,860 --> 00:03:17,960
with clear rules and responsibilities for the effective

71
00:03:17,960 --> 00:03:20,520
discharge of responsibilities in this regard.
